{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/Ryan Gosling.txt"},"lines":{"text":"Ryan Thomas Gosling, actor, musician, producer, director (born 12 November 1980 in London, ON). Ryan Gosling started out as a child actor before giving a breakthrough performance in the Sundance-winning indie drama The Believer in 2001. He has since created, in the words of the New York Times' Dennis Lim, \"a whole gallery of sensitive, intelligent, anguished young men, often with hipster tendencies or dark sides.\" An A-list Hollywood star, he has proven equally adept at comedy ( Lars and the Real Girl, Crazy, Stupid, Love., The Nice Guys, The Big Short), drama (The Notebook, Half Nelson, Blue Valentine, The Ides of March, First Man) and science fiction (Blade Runner 2049). He has received two Oscar nominations and won a Golden Globe in 2017 for his lead role in the musical La La Land.\n"},"line_number":5,"absolute_offset":45,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"2017"},"start":746,"end":750}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/Ryan Gosling.txt"},"lines":{"text":"Gosling scored the starring role in Québécois director Denis Villeneuve's highly anticipated Blade Runner sequel, Blade Runner 2049 (2017). He appeared opposite Michael Fassbender and Natalie Portman in Terence Malick's Song to Song (2017), about a love triangle set in the music scene in Austin, Texas. Gosling also played American astronaut Neil Armstrong in La La Land director Damien Chazelle's biopic about Armstrong, First Man.\n"},"line_number":59,"absolute_offset":10823,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"2017"},"start":135,"end":139},{"match":{"text":"2017"},"start":236,"end":240}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/Ryan Gosling.txt"},"lines":{"text":"- Best Performance by an Actor in a Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy (La La Land), Golden Globe Awards (2017)\n"},"line_number":117,"absolute_offset":14758,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"2017"},"start":108,"end":112}]}}
